TASK: Replace from-scratch encoder with pretrained MMS acoustic backbone, 
keep CTC head from the previous diagnostic

CONTEXT
=======
Previous diagnostic (CTC head on from-scratch 3-layer Transformer encoder, 
d=128, ~195 single-word clips) confirmed encoder collapse: trained encoder 
output is bit-identical (cosine=1.0000) across all probe clips regardless 
of input audio. Root cause: from-scratch transformer has insufficient 
gradient signal at this data scale to learn non-trivial audio 
representations. Fix: replace random-init encoder with a pretrained 
multilingual speech backbone that already has general acoustic 
representations, so fine-tuning only needs to adapt to Cebuano specifics.

TASK
====
1. Load facebook/mms-1b-all or a smaller MMS/wav2vec2-XLSR variant 
   (research current best small-footprint option — prioritize one with 
   Cebuano ("ceb") or Southeast Asian/Austronesian language coverage in 
   pretraining data) via HuggingFace transformers.
2. Replace src/models/encoder.py's AudioFeatureExtractor + Transformer 
   encoder with the pretrained backbone's feature extractor + encoder 
   stack. Freeze all backbone layers except the last 2-4 transformer 
   layers (standard low-resource fine-tuning recipe).
3. Keep the CTC head (src/models/ctc_head.py) from the previous 
   diagnostic, adjusted for the backbone's hidden dim (likely much 
   larger than 128 — check backbone config).
4. Fine-tune on current dataset (whatever's collected as of this run — 
   confirm exact clip count/split before starting).
5. Run the same encoder-collapse probe as before: pairwise cosine 
   similarity of encoder output across held-out clips. This is the 
   PRIMARY signal — confirm collapse is resolved (cosine should vary 
   meaningfully, not sit at ~1.0000) before looking at WER/CER at all.
6. Report: collapse probe result, greedy-decode holdout table (same 
   format as before), aggregate WER/CER, and model size (pre-shrink).

CONSTRAINTS
===========
- Don't worry about the final ~8.9MB footprint yet — that's a later 
  distillation/quantization step. This run is purely to validate the 
  backbone fixes the audio-conditioning problem.
- Save as a new checkpoint line, don't overwrite ctc/ or v026/.